course: dictionary
lesson: 166
title: One word, many meanings: age
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: The word age can mean different things. The words around it show you which meaning is right. «Your dose depends on your age and weight» means how many years you have lived, because a dose changes with the years you have lived, just as it changes with your weight.
explain: «I waited for ages» does not mean you waited for a number of years. Ages here means a very long time. Check by swapping in your meaning: «I waited for a very long time» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «Stone Age people in Britain did not write» uses age to mean a long period of history. The Stone Age is one of these long periods, and it is a big clue that age can name a time in the past. To age is a different use: it means to grow older, as in «Dogs age faster than people.»
fact: Age, as a noun, means how many years you have lived.
fact: An age is a long period of history, such as the Stone Age or the Ice Age.
fact: «Ages» means a very long time: «I waited for ages».
fact: To age, as a verb, means to grow older.
fact: Writing came to Britain with the Romans about 2,000 years ago, so Stone Age people in Britain could not write.
exercise: «Your dose depends on your age and weight.» In this sentence, age means | A very long time | A long period of history | To grow older | *How many years you have lived
exercise: «I waited for ages.» What does ages mean? | A period of history | *A very long time | To grow older | Your age in years
exercise: In the list «a lovely little old round red French wooden toy box», which word tells the age? | lovely | *old | red | round
test: «Stone Age people in Britain did not write.» What is the Stone Age? | A type of stone | *A long period of history | The year you were born | A very old man
test: What does to age mean? | To sleep for a long time | To count the years | To break something | *To grow older
exam: Mia and Sam are the same age, so they | have both been waiting for ages | have both lived in the Stone Age | must be twins | *have lived the same number of years
